asr-000991
01:02:10.020 --> 01:02:12.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Maraming salamat po, Madam Speaker.

asr-000992
01:02:12.020 --> 01:02:15.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Good day to our colleagues in this Chamber,

asr-000993
01:02:15.020 --> 01:02:17.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: to the Distinguished Sponsor,

asr-000994
01:02:17.020 --> 01:02:22.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: and to the Secretary of the Department of Social Welfare and Development, Secretary Rex,

asr-000995
01:02:22.020 --> 01:02:26.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: together with the heads of its attached and supervised agency,

asr-000996
01:02:26.020 --> 01:02:28.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: who are with us as in this session.

asr-000997
01:02:28.020 --> 01:02:31.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Before anything else, Madam Speaker,

asr-000998
01:02:31.020 --> 01:02:34.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: let me place on record my appreciation,

asr-000999
01:02:34.020 --> 01:02:40.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: and I am certain that this is shared by the Chamber for the work of the Department and its people.

asr-001000
01:02:40.020 --> 01:02:48.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: The 4P's alone has helped 1.77 million households graduate to self-sufficiency since 2022,

asr-001001
01:02:48.020 --> 01:02:55.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: and 7.24 million children of beneficiary households have completed basic education.

asr-001002
01:02:55.020 --> 01:02:57.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Through the Quick Response Fund,

asr-001003
01:02:57.020 --> 01:03:00.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: and its network of over a thousand warehouses,

asr-001004
01:03:00.020 --> 01:03:08.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: the Department continues to be the first responder of our people in times of disaster.

asr-001005
01:03:08.020 --> 01:03:11.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: This is not a Department we come here to fault.

asr-001006
01:03:11.020 --> 01:03:14.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: This is a Department we come here to strengthen and to support.

asr-001007
01:03:14.020 --> 01:03:21.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Ngayon, Madam Speaker, para sa una kong katanungan, nalagyan ko po ng konting konteksto.

asr-001008
01:03:21.020 --> 01:03:26.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Poverty incidents among the population fell to 9.7%.

asr-001009
01:03:27.020 --> 01:03:29.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: In 2025.

asr-001010
01:03:29.020 --> 01:03:35.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: But this figure does not yet reflect the Middle East-linked oil price shock

asr-001011
01:03:35.020 --> 01:03:41.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: projected by PIDS to add up to 1.34 million poor Filipinos,

asr-001012
01:03:41.020 --> 01:03:46.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: and the Philippines' new upper middle-income country classification,

asr-001013
01:03:46.020 --> 01:03:50.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: which may require the poverty line used for cross-country comparison

asr-001014
01:03:50.020 --> 01:03:56.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: to rise from 4.20 dollars a day to 8.3 dollars a day,

asr-001015
01:03:56.020 --> 01:04:01.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: potentially tripling the estimated incidence.

asr-001016
01:04:01.020 --> 01:04:02.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Ngayon, Madam Speaker,

asr-001017
01:04:02.020 --> 01:04:08.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: given the PIDS projection that the ongoing oil price shock

asr-001018
01:04:08.020 --> 01:04:14.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: could push as many as 1.34 million additional Filipinos into poverty,

asr-001019
01:04:14.020 --> 01:04:18.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: and the possible upward revision of the poverty threshold

asr-001020
01:04:18.020 --> 01:04:24.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: following our recent reclassification as an upper middle-income country,

asr-001021
01:04:24.020 --> 01:04:30.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: was the Department's 2027 budget calibrated against these emerging risks

asr-001022
01:04:30.020 --> 01:04:36.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: or prepared solely on the basis of the 2025 preliminary poverty rate?

asr-001023
01:04:36.020 --> 01:04:48.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: May we repeat the question again, Madam Speaker, Your Honor?

asr-001024
01:04:48.020 --> 01:04:52.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Madam Speaker, ayon po sa datos, bumaba daw po ang poverty incidence

asr-001025
01:04:52.020 --> 01:04:59.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: sa ating populasyon to 9.7 percent in 2025.

asr-001026
01:04:59.020 --> 01:05:05.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Ngunit, Madam Speaker, hindi pa po na-re-reflect sa figure na ito

asr-001027
01:05:05.020 --> 01:05:09.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: ang epekto ng Middle East oil price shock,

asr-001028
01:05:09.020 --> 01:05:13.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: at ayon po sa mga pagsusuri ng PIDS,

asr-001029
01:05:13.020 --> 01:05:18.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: maaaring dumagdag po ang dami ng ating mga kababayan na mahihirap.

asr-001030
01:05:18.020 --> 01:05:20.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Maaaring dumagdag po ito ng 1.34 million.

asr-001031
01:05:20.020 --> 01:05:28.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: At dahil nagkaroon po ng upper middle-income classification ang ating bansa,

asr-001032
01:05:28.020 --> 01:05:33.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: yung ating threshold for poverty line cross-country comparison

asr-001033
01:05:33.020 --> 01:05:38.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: maaaring umangat from 4.20 dollars a day to 8.30 dollars a day,

asr-001034
01:05:38.020 --> 01:05:40.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: tripling the estimated incidence.

asr-001035
01:05:40.020 --> 01:05:43.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So ang katanungan ko po, Madam Speaker,

asr-001036
01:05:43.020 --> 01:05:47.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: given the projection ng ating oil price shock,

asr-001037
01:05:47.020 --> 01:05:49.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: at hindi pa po ito na-factor in,

asr-001038
01:05:49.020 --> 01:05:52.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: sa 9.7 percent poverty incidence rate,

asr-001039
01:05:52.020 --> 01:05:57.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: at dahil na-re-classify po tayo to upper middle-income classification,

asr-001040
01:05:57.020 --> 01:06:02.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: gusto ko po malaman kung ang budget ng DSWD for 2027,

asr-001041
01:06:02.020 --> 01:06:07.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: na-calibrate na po ba ito considering these emerging risks?

asr-001042
01:06:07.020 --> 01:06:15.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Or hinanda po ba siya on the basis of the 2025 preliminary poverty rate?

asr-001043
01:06:15.020 --> 01:06:18.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Madam Speaker, first of all, Your Honor,

asr-001044
01:06:18.020 --> 01:06:23.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: what the figure that is being considered as of the moment

asr-001045
01:06:23.020 --> 01:06:26.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: is not the current figure which is below 10 percent,

asr-001046
01:06:26.020 --> 01:06:31.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: but rather the 2023 figure which is at 15 percent.

asr-001047
01:06:31.020 --> 01:06:33.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: That's the basis.

asr-001048
01:06:33.020 --> 01:06:41.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: And looking forward to what was mentioned on the current crisis

asr-001049
01:06:41.020 --> 01:06:46.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: that we are experiencing,

asr-001050
01:06:48.020 --> 01:06:53.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: AICS was tapped to address this

asr-001051
01:06:53.020 --> 01:07:00.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: by the program we call Uplift.

asr-001052
01:07:00.020 --> 01:07:09.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: There's a tap-up as far as four-piece beneficiaries are concerned

asr-001053
01:07:09.020 --> 01:07:16.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: to further augment their benefits

asr-001054
01:07:16.020 --> 01:07:21.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: because of this situation, Your Honor, Madam Speaker.

asr-001055
01:07:21.020 --> 01:07:24.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Madam Speaker, nabanggit po ng ating distinguished sponsor

asr-001056
01:07:24.020 --> 01:07:29.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: na pinagbasihan po natin dito ang poverty incidence rate ng 2023,

asr-001057
01:07:29.020 --> 01:07:33.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: the crafting of the current proposed budget for 2027.

asr-001058
01:07:33.020 --> 01:07:35.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: As I've mentioned, Madam Speaker,

asr-001059
01:07:35.020 --> 01:07:38.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: there are current emerging risks that our country is facing

asr-001060
01:07:38.020 --> 01:07:40.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: aside from the Middle East crisis.

asr-001061
01:07:40.020 --> 01:07:44.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Of course, meron pa pong inflation among several other problems.

asr-001062
01:07:44.020 --> 01:07:48.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So ang tanong ko po naman ng kasunodan pong tanong, Madam Speaker,

asr-001063
01:07:48.020 --> 01:07:54.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: should any of these risks materialize within the upcoming fiscal year,

asr-001064
01:07:54.020 --> 01:07:58.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: meron po bang contingency financing plan ang ating departamento

asr-001065
01:07:58.020 --> 01:08:03.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: kung sakaling mapatunayan na ang nararanasan ng ating mga kababayan sa ground

asr-001066
01:08:03.020 --> 01:08:06.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: ay mas manubha pa po kumpara noong taong 2023?

asr-001067
01:08:06.020 --> 01:08:09.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: As what we have done for this year,

asr-001068
01:08:09.020 --> 01:08:13.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: AICS was tapped to augment

asr-001069
01:08:13.020 --> 01:08:19.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: the benefits that the 4Ps beneficiaries are receiving

asr-001070
01:08:19.020 --> 01:08:22.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: under the program Uplift.

asr-001071
01:08:22.020 --> 01:08:27.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: The possibility of having such again

asr-001072
01:08:27.020 --> 01:08:36.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: would certainly be, I think, a repeat of the intervention may be done

asr-001073
01:08:36.020 --> 01:08:40.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: to address the situation again in case there is another crisis

asr-001074
01:08:40.020 --> 01:08:43.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: or for that matter, Madam Speaker.

asr-001075
01:08:43.020 --> 01:08:46.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: For my next set of questions, Madam Speaker,

asr-001076
01:08:46.020 --> 01:08:51.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: may mga katanungan lang rin naman po ako tungkol naman po sa ating four-piece program.

asr-001077
01:08:51.020 --> 01:08:55.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Tulad ng nabanggit po kanina ni Congressman Presley,

asr-001078
01:08:55.020 --> 01:09:01.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: may nabanggit po siya kung saan may mga pagkakataon na maaaring nagkaroon po ng onting overpayments

asr-001079
01:09:01.020 --> 01:09:03.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: tuwing nagkakaroon ng delisting delays.

asr-001080
01:09:03.020 --> 01:09:09.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And nauunawaan ko po ang problema ito ng departamento dahil nakita ko rin po mismo

asr-001081
01:09:09.020 --> 01:09:12.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: at natuklasan ko po mismo on the ground,

asr-001082
01:09:12.020 --> 01:09:17.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: na may mga pagkakataon kung saan malaki po yung caseload ng ating mga social worker

asr-001083
01:09:17.020 --> 01:09:21.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: kaya hindi po maiwasan na magkakaroon po tayo ng mga delays.

asr-001084
01:09:21.020 --> 01:09:24.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: On top of that, mayroon rin delays sa CBMS

asr-001085
01:09:24.020 --> 01:09:29.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: kaya may mga times na delayed po talaga ang ating delisting.

asr-001086
01:09:29.020 --> 01:09:39.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So, ako po, Madam Speaker, gusto ko pong malaman kung ano po ang mga hakbang na ginagawa ng ating departamento.

asr-001087
01:09:39.020 --> 01:09:41.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Meron po ba tayong mga...

asr-001088
01:09:42.020 --> 01:09:49.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: mechanisms or system upgrades para maiwasan po ang mga instances of delays

asr-001089
01:09:49.020 --> 01:09:56.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: pagdating po sa delisting ng mga households na nakita na nating self-sufficient or for whatever reasons as the case may be.

asr-001090
01:09:56.020 --> 01:09:59.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: As mentioned earlier, Madam Speaker, Your Honor,

asr-001091
01:09:59.020 --> 01:10:10.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: the department is working on a new program that would provide almost a real-time tracking system.

asr-001092
01:10:10.020 --> 01:10:11.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: In this case,

asr-001093
01:10:11.020 --> 01:10:23.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: concerns on those mentioned will be outrightly addressed through this digitalization program, Your Honor, Madam Speaker.

asr-001094
01:10:23.020 --> 01:10:30.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Madam Speaker, nagpapasalamat po ako sa ating departamento dahil mag-i-institutionalize tayo ng real-time tagging system

asr-001095
01:10:30.020 --> 01:10:38.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: para maiwasan po ang delays sa pagdelist ng mga beneficiaries na kailangan na pong graduate.

asr-001096
01:10:38.020 --> 01:10:39.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And on top of this question,

asr-001097
01:10:39.020 --> 01:10:40.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: naalala ko nga po, Madam Speaker,

asr-001098
01:10:40.020 --> 01:10:43.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: noong 19th Congress,

asr-001099
01:10:43.020 --> 01:10:48.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: nakasama po namin ang department nung inaaral namin ang posibilidad

asr-001100
01:10:48.020 --> 01:10:52.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: na i-empower naman po rin ang mga parent leader naman ng 4Ps.

asr-001101
01:10:52.020 --> 01:10:55.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Dahil for the longest time, tulad ng banggit ko po kanina,

asr-001102
01:10:55.020 --> 01:10:58.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: ang ating mga city and municipal link,

asr-001103
01:10:58.020 --> 01:11:02.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: napakarami po na households ang kanilang inaasikaso.

asr-001104
01:11:02.020 --> 01:11:04.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: If I remember correctly,

asr-001105
01:11:04.020 --> 01:11:08.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: it can go as high as, a city or municipal link could cater to around

asr-001106
01:11:08.020 --> 01:11:13.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: more than 500 households in some instances.

asr-001107
01:11:13.020 --> 01:11:16.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: At naniniwala po ako na siguro bumaba na po yung numero na yun.

asr-001108
01:11:16.020 --> 01:11:24.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Gusto ko po malaman ngayon kung ano yung stance ng department pagdating po sa aming panukala

asr-001109
01:11:24.020 --> 01:11:28.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: na i-empower po yung mga parent leader para matulungan po yung department

asr-001110
01:11:28.020 --> 01:11:33.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: sa pag-verify ng mga households na kailangan ng graduate mula sa programa.

asr-001111
01:11:33.020 --> 01:11:37.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And of course, kinikilala rin po ng departamento sa kanilang IRR yung kakalagahan.

asr-001112
01:11:38.020 --> 01:11:41.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: ng mga parent leader ng mga 4Ps.

asr-001113
01:11:41.020 --> 01:11:47.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: The proposal, Your Honor, Madam Speaker, is very much acceptable to the department.

asr-001114
01:11:47.020 --> 01:11:57.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Fortunately, the department cannot compensate these leaders as well.

asr-001115
01:11:57.020 --> 01:12:00.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: There's no additional budget for that.

asr-001116
01:12:00.020 --> 01:12:03.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Maraming maraming salamat po, Mr. Distinguished Sponsor,

asr-001117
01:12:03.020 --> 01:12:07.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: dahil nananatili pa rin po ang suporta ng departamento.

asr-001118
01:12:07.020 --> 01:12:11.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: At kinikilala pa rin nila ang kahalagan ng mga parent leader ng 4Ps

asr-001119
01:12:11.020 --> 01:12:15.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: pagdating po sa pagpaunlad ng ating programa.

asr-001120
01:12:15.020 --> 01:12:18.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Ngayon, Madam Speaker, may mga katanungan rin po ako

asr-001121
01:12:18.020 --> 01:12:22.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: pagdating naman po sa status ng mga wait-listed households.

asr-001122
01:12:22.020 --> 01:12:31.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Dahil alam naman po nating lahat, noong nag-transition ang listahanan to CBMS,

asr-001123
01:12:31.020 --> 01:12:35.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: may mga households po sa CBMS na hindi mahanap sa listahanan.

asr-001124
01:12:35.020 --> 01:12:36.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Ayon po.

asr-001125
01:12:36.020 --> 01:12:39.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Ayon po sa datos na meron ako dito,

asr-001126
01:12:39.020 --> 01:12:43.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: pagdating po sa qualified set 12 beneficiaries,

asr-001127
01:12:43.020 --> 01:12:50.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: nagkaroon po ng as much as 434,069 households who were wait-listed.

asr-001128
01:12:50.020 --> 01:13:00.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: 166,251 were endorsed by the Social Registry Office to be included in the 4Ps CBMS.

asr-001129
01:13:00.020 --> 01:13:02.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So yung tanong ko po, Madam Speaker,

asr-001130
01:13:02.020 --> 01:13:04.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: dito sa mga wait-listed households on the 4Ps,

asr-001131
01:13:04.020 --> 01:13:07.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: dito sa mga wait-listed households under set 12,

asr-001132
01:13:07.020 --> 01:13:13.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: ilan na lang po dito ang natitira for special revalidation?

asr-001133
01:13:13.020 --> 01:13:18.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: For all those wait-listed,

asr-001134
01:13:18.020 --> 01:13:31.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: the 434,069, only 59,462 were not identified as of yet.

asr-001135
01:13:31.020 --> 01:13:33.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: So the rest are already in.

asr-001136
01:13:34.020 --> 01:13:41.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: And will be part of the 3.5 million beneficiaries for next year.

asr-001137
01:13:41.020 --> 01:13:46.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Madam Speaker, pwede ko rin po bang malaman kung yung 59,000 households nito,

asr-001138
01:13:46.020 --> 01:13:53.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: may certain areas ba kung saan concentrated yung population ng mga households na ito?

asr-001139
01:13:53.020 --> 01:13:58.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Dahil maaaring nasa geographic areas sila na mahirap abutin,

asr-001140
01:13:58.020 --> 01:14:00.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: kaya siguro mahirap ma-validate.

asr-001141
01:14:00.020 --> 01:14:03.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So, naka-curious po ako, Madam Speaker, kung saan po yung,

asr-001142
01:14:03.020 --> 01:14:06.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: naka-concentrate yung numero na ito?

asr-001143
01:14:06.020 --> 01:14:09.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And if I may also ask, Madam Speaker,

asr-001144
01:14:09.020 --> 01:14:17.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: gaano na po katagal naghihintay ang mga households na wait-listed for special revalidation?

asr-001145
01:14:33.020 --> 01:14:49.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: So the validation process started early part of this year.

asr-001146
01:14:49.020 --> 01:14:55.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: And the number or the 59,000 is spread all over.

asr-001147
01:14:55.020 --> 01:15:00.560
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: And they were, I think, advice was given.

asr-001148
01:15:00.560 --> 01:15:06.800
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: that the first thing that they can do is to approach their respective local government units

asr-001149
01:15:06.800 --> 01:15:12.060
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: for purposes of identification and validation, Your Honor, Madam Speaker.

asr-001150
01:15:12.660 --> 01:15:20.180
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Madam Speaker, if I may also ask, did the Philippine Statistics Authority commit to a certain target timeline

asr-001151
01:15:20.180 --> 01:15:26.840
Rep. JC M. Abalos: kung kailan po nila maaaring matapos ang kanilang special validation ng mga 59,000 households?

asr-001152
01:15:26.840 --> 01:15:33.040
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: They committed. Unfortunately, they're short of the target, Your Honor, Madam Speaker.

asr-001153
01:15:33.680 --> 01:15:39.200
Rep. JC M. Abalos: My question, Madam Speaker, is is there a specific target date in mind?

asr-001154
01:15:39.500 --> 01:15:45.520
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Kailan po kaya, when is the department expecting the PSA to complete this?

asr-001155
01:15:45.820 --> 01:15:49.840
Rep. JC M. Abalos: I understand po dahil iba po yung trabaho ng departamento sa PSA

asr-001156
01:15:49.840 --> 01:15:56.840
Rep. JC M. Abalos: at nagtutulungan lamang po ang PSA at ng DSWD pagdating sa special validation.

asr-001157
01:15:56.840 --> 01:16:03.180
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So yung tanong ko lang po, may kinamit po kaya ang PSA sa DSWD kung kailan matatapos ang validation?

asr-001158
01:16:03.180 --> 01:16:09.800
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: They informed the department that they will be done with this by end of September, Your Honor.

asr-001159
01:16:10.220 --> 01:16:13.120
Rep. JC M. Abalos: By end of September. Maraming salamat po, Madam Speaker.

asr-001160
01:16:13.640 --> 01:16:20.120
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And then for my next question, nakasanayan na po kasi and I think it's been a practice for quite some time

asr-001161
01:16:20.120 --> 01:16:26.760
Rep. JC M. Abalos: na yung target coverage ng 4Ps ay pumapalo ng mga 4.4 million households.

asr-001162
01:16:26.840 --> 01:16:34.420
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And natuklasan po natin na beginning 2026, naging 3.5 million po ang ating target.

asr-001163
01:16:35.000 --> 01:16:43.220
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So maaari ko po ba malaman kung ano po yung basis natin for this reduced target under the proposed 2027 budget?

asr-001164
01:16:46.580 --> 01:16:53.500
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: There's a continuous decrease in the poverty incidence, Your Honor, Madam Speaker.

asr-001165
01:16:53.500 --> 01:16:56.500
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: The very reason why the targeted beneficiary.

asr-001166
01:16:56.840 --> 01:16:58.200
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: That is also lowered down.

asr-001167
01:16:58.980 --> 01:17:04.560
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Despite the decrease in the poverty incidence,

asr-001168
01:17:04.960 --> 01:17:15.180
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: the department still identified the 10% of the near poor group to be covered under this program.

asr-001169
01:17:15.880 --> 01:17:18.560
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: So it's not totally poorest,

asr-001170
01:17:18.560 --> 01:17:26.160
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: but the same way, a certain percentage of the near poor, Your Honor, Madam Speaker.

asr-001171
01:17:26.840 --> 01:17:33.720
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So is it safe to say, Madam Speaker, that the basis for lowering the target number of households for the 4Ps program

asr-001172
01:17:33.720 --> 01:17:37.360
Rep. JC M. Abalos: is based on the prevailing poverty incidence rate?

asr-001173
01:17:37.780 --> 01:17:39.260
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Yes, Your Honor, Madam Speaker.

asr-001174
01:17:40.820 --> 01:17:42.520
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Madam Speaker, para sa...

asr-001175
01:17:42.520 --> 01:17:44.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: At 15%.

asr-001176
01:17:44.020 --> 01:17:46.620
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Yes, 15% yung basis po.

asr-001177
01:17:46.620 --> 01:17:56.760
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And then, if I may ask, Madam Speaker, is the poverty incidence rate typically based on the family income expenditure survey?

asr-001178
01:17:56.760 --> 01:17:58.100
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Conducted by the PSA?

asr-001179
01:17:58.180 --> 01:18:03.040
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Ano po kaya yung nagiging pinaka-statistical basis kapag kinukomplete po natin ito?

asr-001180
01:18:03.780 --> 01:18:11.640
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: It's the PSA process, Your Honor, Madam Speaker,

asr-001181
01:18:12.640 --> 01:18:16.200
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: that they utilize the family income and expenditure survey.

asr-001182
01:18:17.440 --> 01:18:20.840
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Madam Speaker, base po sa aking pananaliksik,

asr-001183
01:18:21.400 --> 01:18:25.140
Rep. JC M. Abalos: natuklas na rin po natin na yung family income expenditure survey

asr-001184
01:18:25.140 --> 01:18:26.740
Rep. JC M. Abalos: is sinasagawa po ito.

asr-001185
01:18:26.760 --> 01:18:28.000
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Every two years.

asr-001186
01:18:28.940 --> 01:18:30.960
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And maybe two or three years.

asr-001187
01:18:31.180 --> 01:18:32.220
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Please correct me if I'm wrong.

asr-001188
01:18:32.440 --> 01:18:33.140
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Every three years.

asr-001189
01:18:33.680 --> 01:18:37.900
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And tulad po ng CBMS, tulad rin po ng family income expenditure survey,

asr-001190
01:18:38.400 --> 01:18:40.760
Rep. JC M. Abalos: dahil meron po tayong three-year cycle na sinusundan,

asr-001191
01:18:41.820 --> 01:18:44.640
Rep. JC M. Abalos: ang pangamba po ng representasyong ito ay

asr-001192
01:18:44.640 --> 01:18:47.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: kung ito po ang ating pagbabasihan,

asr-001193
01:18:48.600 --> 01:18:51.660
Rep. JC M. Abalos: marami po kasing pwede mangyari sa loob ng tatlong taon.

asr-001194
01:18:51.660 --> 01:18:54.960
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Hindi po natin alam kung magkakaroon ng isa pang pandemia

asr-001195
01:18:54.960 --> 01:18:56.740
Rep. JC M. Abalos: o isa pang crisis,

asr-001196
01:18:56.760 --> 01:18:58.860
Rep. JC M. Abalos: tungkol sa Middle East oil crisis.

asr-001197
01:18:59.460 --> 01:19:00.380
Rep. JC M. Abalos: For example,

asr-001198
01:19:01.100 --> 01:19:03.720
Rep. JC M. Abalos: so what I'm trying to say, Madam Speaker,

asr-001199
01:19:04.200 --> 01:19:09.100
Rep. JC M. Abalos: is that pagamat maganda na nagkakaroon po tayo ng mga census

asr-001200
01:19:09.100 --> 01:19:14.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: and ng mga survey para imeasure kung ilan sa ating mga kababayan

asr-001201
01:19:14.020 --> 01:19:15.880
Rep. JC M. Abalos: ang nakakaranas ng kahirapan,

asr-001202
01:19:16.560 --> 01:19:18.780
Rep. JC M. Abalos: marami pong pwedeng mangyari in a span of three years.

asr-001203
01:19:19.180 --> 01:19:23.640
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And we always want the budget to reflect the existing realities

asr-001204
01:19:23.640 --> 01:19:25.260
Rep. JC M. Abalos: that happen on the ground.

asr-001205
01:19:25.260 --> 01:19:26.620
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Kaya nabanggit ko po kanina,

asr-001206
01:19:26.760 --> 01:19:27.340
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Madam Speaker,

asr-001207
01:19:27.900 --> 01:19:30.700
Rep. JC M. Abalos: na hindi pa natin natatake into account

asr-001208
01:19:30.700 --> 01:19:32.580
Rep. JC M. Abalos: yung Middle East crisis,

asr-001209
01:19:33.200 --> 01:19:34.700
Rep. JC M. Abalos: yung oil price shock,

asr-001210
01:19:35.440 --> 01:19:36.140
Rep. JC M. Abalos: yung inflation.

asr-001211
01:19:36.720 --> 01:19:39.300
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So gusto ko lang po sana hingiin yung commitment

asr-001212
01:19:39.300 --> 01:19:41.860
Rep. JC M. Abalos: ng ating sponsor at ng ating department

asr-001213
01:19:41.860 --> 01:19:45.740
Rep. JC M. Abalos: na mag-communicate constantly, of course,

asr-001214
01:19:46.260 --> 01:19:49.640
Rep. JC M. Abalos: with the DBM and the DepDev as the case may be

asr-001215
01:19:49.640 --> 01:19:52.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: kung sakaling nakita po nila on the ground

asr-001216
01:19:52.020 --> 01:19:55.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: na malaki na po ang impact ng mga problemang ito.

asr-001217
01:19:55.940 --> 01:19:58.060
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Considering na hindi po siya factored in

asr-001218
01:19:58.060 --> 01:20:00.000
Rep. JC M. Abalos: sa planning stage po ng ating budget.

asr-001219
01:20:01.160 --> 01:20:04.920
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: The department agrees to that, Madam Speaker, Your Honor.

asr-001220
01:20:05.700 --> 01:20:16.680
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: In fact, we have the assistance for individuals in crisis situation

asr-001221
01:20:16.680 --> 01:20:24.200
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: which usually the immediate program that can address

asr-001222
01:20:24.200 --> 01:20:25.900
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: temporary relief.

asr-001223
01:20:25.940 --> 01:20:27.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: For these cases.

asr-001224
01:20:27.940 --> 01:20:33.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: And the department can as well come up with temporary programs

asr-001225
01:20:33.940 --> 01:20:37.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: like what they have done as far as uplift is concerned,

asr-001226
01:20:37.940 --> 01:20:39.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Your Honor, Madam Speaker.

asr-001227
01:20:39.940 --> 01:20:46.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: And that could be duplicated or scaled up just if necessary,

asr-001228
01:20:46.940 --> 01:20:48.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: I suppose, Madam Speaker, Your Honor.

asr-001229
01:20:48.940 --> 01:20:54.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Madam Speaker, gusto ko rin po ipaalam sa ating distinguished sponsor at sa department,

asr-001230
01:20:54.940 --> 01:20:55.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: at sigurado po akong

asr-001231
01:20:55.940 --> 01:20:57.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: alam ito ng department

asr-001232
01:20:57.940 --> 01:21:00.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: na napasa na po ng mababang kapulungan

asr-001233
01:21:00.940 --> 01:21:05.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: ang ledak priority measure na pagtibayan pa po ang Four-Peace Act.

asr-001234
01:21:05.940 --> 01:21:09.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And dito ini-institutionalize po natin ang first 1,000 days,

asr-001235
01:21:09.940 --> 01:21:12.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: ang rice subsidy, for example.

asr-001236
01:21:12.940 --> 01:21:16.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So gusto ko lang po itanong sa ating sponsor at sa ating department na

asr-001237
01:21:16.940 --> 01:21:22.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: considering na may onting pagbawas sa pondo ng Four-Peace program,

asr-001238
01:21:22.940 --> 01:21:25.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: intact pa rin po ba ang mga programang ito

asr-001239
01:21:25.940 --> 01:21:26.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: para sa ating mga kababayan?

asr-001240
01:21:26.940 --> 01:21:29.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: As far as Four-Peace, Your Honor, Madam Speaker,

asr-001241
01:21:29.940 --> 01:21:37.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: it's still sufficient considering that the number targeted is smaller than what we have right now,

asr-001242
01:21:37.940 --> 01:21:39.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: currently here.

asr-001243
01:21:39.940 --> 01:21:42.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And then, Madam Speaker, for my next set of questions,

asr-001244
01:21:42.940 --> 01:21:47.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: tatanong naman po ako tungkol sa Supplemental Feeding Program and Child Nutrition.

asr-001245
01:21:47.940 --> 01:21:49.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Performance data show mixed results.

asr-001246
01:21:49.940 --> 01:21:54.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: The percentage of malnourished children with improved nutritional status reached

asr-001247
01:21:54.940 --> 01:22:00.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: 78.92% against a 70.05% target in 2025.

asr-001248
01:22:00.940 --> 01:22:08.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: But only 61,371 of an expected higher cohort were confirmed served

asr-001249
01:22:08.940 --> 01:22:12.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: under the tighter 2025 budget window.

asr-001250
01:22:12.940 --> 01:22:18.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Madam Speaker, the reduction of SFP funding by a third appears to walk back

asr-001251
01:22:18.940 --> 01:22:24.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: the extended 180 feeding cycle achieved in 2026.

asr-001252
01:22:24.940 --> 01:22:30.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Can the good sponsor confirm whether reverting toward a 120-day cycle

asr-001253
01:22:30.940 --> 01:22:36.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: for 1.9 million children is expected to affect nutritional outcomes

asr-001254
01:22:36.940 --> 01:22:40.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: and how this squares with our national nutrition policy?

asr-001255
01:22:44.940 --> 01:22:52.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Technically, it will be much better for the department if the 2026 level

asr-001256
01:22:52.940 --> 01:22:56.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: can be restored for 2027, Madam Speaker, Your Honor.

asr-001257
01:22:56.940 --> 01:23:00.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So, Madam Speaker, with the reduced allocation,

asr-001258
01:23:00.940 --> 01:23:04.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: may I know how many feeding days can the DSWD sustain?

asr-001259
01:23:04.940 --> 01:23:10.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And if it's possible for us to maintain the 180-day cycle achieved in 2026,

asr-001260
01:23:10.940 --> 01:23:16.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: or would funding constraints require a return to 120 days?

asr-001261
01:23:16.940 --> 01:23:20.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: The estimate goes down to 120 days, Your Honor, Madam Speaker.

asr-001262
01:23:20.940 --> 01:23:24.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Maraming salamat po, Mr. Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-001263
01:23:24.940 --> 01:23:30.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Para sa aking susunod naman pong katanungan, gusto ko lang pong ipaalam

asr-001264
01:23:30.940 --> 01:23:34.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: sa departamento ang aking mga obserbasyon po pagdating po sa CBMS.

asr-001265
01:23:34.940 --> 01:23:40.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Alam naman po nating lahat, napakahalaga ng CBMS dahil

asr-001266
01:23:40.940 --> 01:23:46.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: nagge-generate po tayo ng aggregated and disaggregated data at the household level,

asr-001267
01:23:46.940 --> 01:23:48.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: at nagsisilbi po itong gabay

asr-001268
01:23:48.940 --> 01:23:56.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: hindi lamang po sa mga lokal na pamahalaan kung hindi lalong-lalo na po sa ating national programs.

asr-001269
01:23:56.940 --> 01:24:02.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So, this year, we learned from the Walang Gutom program

asr-001270
01:24:02.940 --> 01:24:10.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: that the DSWD notified the PSA that we have 238 households

asr-001271
01:24:10.940 --> 01:24:14.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: with unidentified or disputed roster members,

asr-001272
01:24:14.940 --> 01:24:18.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: and 128 households that their LGUs,

asr-001273
01:24:18.940 --> 01:24:22.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: that LGUs confirmed are no longer residing in the area surveyed.

asr-001274
01:24:22.940 --> 01:24:26.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Are these figures drawn from the full Walang Gutom program beneficiary list

asr-001275
01:24:26.940 --> 01:24:30.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: or only a sample from a specific region?

asr-001276
01:24:34.940 --> 01:24:36.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: It's the whole, Your Honor, Madam Speaker.

asr-001277
01:24:36.940 --> 01:24:42.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Madam Speaker, gusto ko po malaman na kung ano po ang mga,

asr-001278
01:24:42.940 --> 01:24:46.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: kung nagkaroon po ba ng talakayan ang DSWD, pati po yung PSA,

asr-001279
01:24:46.940 --> 01:24:52.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: para maiwasan po yung discrepancies sa pag-identify ng mga beneficiaries

asr-001280
01:24:52.940 --> 01:24:56.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: na hindi pala dapat nasasali doon.

asr-001281
01:24:56.940 --> 01:25:00.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Dahil naiintindihan ko po na ang pinagbabasihan lamang ng DSWD

asr-001282
01:25:00.940 --> 01:25:04.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: ay ang ibinibigay po sa kanila ng ating CBMS.

asr-001283
01:25:04.940 --> 01:25:08.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: That's why the department, Madam Speaker, Your Honor,

asr-001284
01:25:08.940 --> 01:25:12.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: continues with the validation process in the field.

asr-001285
01:25:12.940 --> 01:25:16.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: There's always an ongoing validation.

asr-001286
01:25:16.940 --> 01:25:26.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: As far as confirming or final acceptance of beneficiaries,

asr-001287
01:25:26.940 --> 01:25:28.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Your Honor, Madam Speaker.

asr-001288
01:25:28.940 --> 01:25:32.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: For my next question, Madam Speaker, gusto ko po itanong rin.

asr-001289
01:25:32.940 --> 01:25:38.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Tungkol naman po ito sa mga contract of service and job order personnel ng DSWD,

asr-001290
01:25:38.940 --> 01:25:42.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: particularly po dito sa mga ating four-piece links.

asr-001291
01:25:42.940 --> 01:25:44.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: With over 17,000 contract of service and job order personnel,

asr-001292
01:25:44.940 --> 01:25:50.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: more than triple the department's authorized permanent positions,

asr-001293
01:25:50.940 --> 01:25:54.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: many of whom have served as four-piece links for over a decade,

asr-001294
01:25:54.940 --> 01:26:00.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: when will the DBM-approved 5,627-item enhanced structure

asr-001295
01:26:00.940 --> 01:26:04.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: be reflected in the staffing summary and funded,

asr-001296
01:26:04.940 --> 01:26:12.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: so that frontline social workers may finally be given security of tenure?

asr-001297
01:26:12.940 --> 01:26:20.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: There's a total of about 5,000 new items for this year, Madam Speaker.

asr-001298
01:26:20.940 --> 01:26:24.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: And the department is on the process of filling up these new items.

asr-001299
01:26:24.940 --> 01:26:30.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: And it is expected another 5,000 will be up for next year again, Madam Speaker, Your Honor.

asr-001300
01:26:30.940 --> 01:26:32.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: This is excellent news, Madam Speaker.

asr-001301
01:26:32.940 --> 01:26:37.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And I commend the department dahil binibigyan po natin ng security of tenure

asr-001302
01:26:37.940 --> 01:26:41.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: ang ating mga social workers na matagal na pong nagsisilbe.

asr-001303
01:26:42.940 --> 01:26:44.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Para po sa ahensya.

asr-001304
01:26:44.940 --> 01:26:48.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Ngayon, for my final question po, Madam Speaker,

asr-001305
01:26:48.940 --> 01:26:54.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: may tanong lang po ako tungkol sa Executive Order No. 51, Series of 2023,

asr-001306
01:26:54.940 --> 01:27:02.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: creating the Special Committee on LGBTQIA plus Affairs under the DSWD.

asr-001307
01:27:02.940 --> 01:27:08.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Yung tanong ko lang po, Madam Speaker, mula nung itinayo ang Special Committee na ito,

asr-001308
01:27:08.940 --> 01:27:12.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: sigurado po ako na marami na pong programa,

asr-001309
01:27:12.940 --> 01:27:20.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: at proyekto, at marami po itong mungkahing activities para pagsilbihan po ang community.

asr-001310
01:27:20.940 --> 01:27:24.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: At nung tinitingnan ko po ang General Appropriations Act,

asr-001311
01:27:24.940 --> 01:27:30.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: wala po ako nakitang item doon kung ano po ang kanilang gagamitan ng pondo

asr-001312
01:27:30.940 --> 01:27:34.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: para mapondohan po ang kanilang mga activity.

asr-001313
01:27:34.940 --> 01:27:40.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Gusto ko lang po malaman kung paano po kaya natin matutulungan ang Special Committee na ito

asr-001314
01:27:40.940 --> 01:27:43.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: para magambanan po nila ang kanilang layunin.

asr-001315
01:27:43.940 --> 01:27:55.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Madam Speaker, Your Honor, I think we need to request the DBM to put a specific item for this unit's program.

asr-001316
01:27:55.940 --> 01:28:01.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: As of now, there's no specific item for that as far as DBM is concerned.

asr-001317
01:28:01.940 --> 01:28:08.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: And funding or expenditure for this purpose is being absorbed by the department itself.

asr-001318
01:28:08.940 --> 01:28:09.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And I to my

asr-001319
01:28:09.940 --> 01:28:11.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: understanding rin po, Madam Speaker,

asr-001320
01:28:11.940 --> 01:28:17.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: sumulat rin po maski pa paano ang department sa DBM asking for a small sum

asr-001321
01:28:17.940 --> 01:28:21.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: to fund the operations of the Special Committee of LGBTQIA Affairs.

asr-001322
01:28:21.940 --> 01:28:27.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So gusto ko lang po kunin sana ang support at ng commitment ng ating sponsor

asr-001323
01:28:27.940 --> 01:28:33.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: for in case later opportunity would come for us to request specific funding

asr-001324
01:28:33.940 --> 01:28:36.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: for the Special Committee on LGBTQIA Affairs,

asr-001325
01:28:36.940 --> 01:28:39.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: susuportahan po ba ng sponsor na magkaroon ng sariling budget

asr-001326
01:28:39.940 --> 01:28:40.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: maski pa paano?

asr-001327
01:28:40.940 --> 01:28:42.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Definitely, Your Honor, Madam Speaker.

asr-001328
01:28:42.940 --> 01:28:45.940
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: We will be supporting such initiative.

asr-001329
01:28:45.940 --> 01:28:50.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Yun lamang po, Madam Speaker, Mr. Distinguished Sponsor at sa Department,

asr-001330
01:28:50.940 --> 01:28:54.880
Rep. JC M. Abalos: maraming maraming salamat at magandang magandang umaga po.

asr-001331
01:28:54.880 --> 01:28:55.950
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Majority Leader?

asr-001332
01:28:55.950 --> 01:28:58.230
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Thank you, Your Honor, Madam Speaker.

