asr-003125
03:02:54.000 --> 03:02:57.000
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: including its attached agencies and corporations.

asr-003126
03:02:58.000 --> 03:03:02.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Thank you very much Madam Speaker,

asr-003127
03:03:02.000 --> 03:03:05.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Honorable Floor Leader,

asr-003128
03:03:05.000 --> 03:03:08.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Magandang umaga po, distinguished colleagues.

asr-003129
03:03:08.000 --> 03:03:13.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: I have the honor to sponsor for consideration of this House,

asr-003130
03:03:13.000 --> 03:03:21.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: the proposed budget of the Department of Health and PhilHealth for Fiscal Year 2027

asr-003131
03:03:21.000 --> 03:03:26.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: in the amount of 263,624,

asr-003132
03:03:26.000 --> 03:03:30.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: 289,000 in new appropriations.

asr-003133
03:03:30.000 --> 03:03:33.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Together with automatic appropriations,

asr-003134
03:03:33.000 --> 03:03:43.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: the Department will administer a total program of 270.565 billion.

asr-003135
03:03:43.000 --> 03:03:47.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The budget answers a clear constitutional command.

asr-003136
03:03:47.000 --> 03:03:54.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Article 2, Section 15 and Article 13, Section 11

asr-003137
03:03:54.000 --> 03:04:00.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: of the Constitution direct the State to protect the right to health

asr-003138
03:04:00.000 --> 03:04:07.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and to make essential health services available to all at all at affordable cost

asr-003139
03:04:07.000 --> 03:04:10.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: with priority for the poor.

asr-003140
03:04:10.000 --> 03:04:17.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Republic Act No. 11223, the Universal Health Care Act,

asr-003141
03:04:17.000 --> 03:04:20.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: is the law that carries out that mandate.

asr-003142
03:04:20.000 --> 03:04:23.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Every peso in this budget serves it.

asr-003143
03:04:24.000 --> 03:04:26.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Of the new appropriations,

asr-003144
03:04:26.000 --> 03:04:33.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: 110.367 billion funds personal services,

asr-003145
03:04:33.000 --> 03:04:41.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: 134.232 billion funds maintenance and other operating expenses,

asr-003146
03:04:41.000 --> 03:04:46.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and 19.026 billion funds capital outlays.

asr-003147
03:04:46.000 --> 03:04:51.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The budget is built for the regions,

asr-003148
03:04:51.000 --> 03:04:54.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: 161.886

asr-003149
03:04:54.000 --> 03:04:56.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: billion,

asr-003150
03:04:56.000 --> 03:05:02.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: or 61% is allocated directly to the 17 regions.

asr-003151
03:05:02.000 --> 03:05:10.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The remaining 101.739 billion supports central operations.

asr-003152
03:05:10.000 --> 03:05:15.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Five operating programs organize the work of the Department.

asr-003153
03:05:15.000 --> 03:05:19.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Number 1, Health Facilities Operation Program,

asr-003154
03:05:19.000 --> 03:05:22.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: 133.335 billion,

asr-003155
03:05:22.000 --> 03:05:24.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: the largest share,

asr-003156
03:05:24.000 --> 03:05:29.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: which sustains our public hospitals and health facilities.

asr-003157
03:05:29.000 --> 03:05:35.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Number 2, Local Health System Support Program,

asr-003158
03:05:35.000 --> 03:05:40.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: 69.613 billion.

asr-003159
03:05:40.000 --> 03:05:43.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Number 3, Social Health Protection Program,

asr-003160
03:05:43.000 --> 03:05:47.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: 27.989 billion.

asr-003161
03:05:47.000 --> 03:05:52.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Number 4, Health Policy and Systems Strengthening Program,

asr-003162
03:05:52.000 --> 03:05:56.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: 9.667 billion.

asr-003163
03:05:56.000 --> 03:05:59.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Number 5, Health Regulatory Program,

asr-003164
03:05:59.000 --> 03:06:02.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: 1.583 billion.

asr-003165
03:06:02.000 --> 03:06:05.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Let me point to where these funds

asr-003166
03:06:05.000 --> 03:06:10.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: do the most direct good for our constituents.

asr-003167
03:06:10.000 --> 03:06:12.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Hospital services,

asr-003168
03:06:12.000 --> 03:06:16.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: 107.291 billion operates.

asr-003169
03:06:16.000 --> 03:06:21.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The DOH, regional hospitals and other health facilities,

asr-003170
03:06:21.000 --> 03:06:31.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and 29, I'm sorry, 28.189 billion operates the DOH hospitals in Metro Manila.

asr-003171
03:06:31.000 --> 03:06:34.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: This is the backbone of the public healthcare,

asr-003172
03:06:34.000 --> 03:06:41.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: the wards and emergency rooms our people depend on.

asr-003173
03:06:41.000 --> 03:06:44.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: For healthcare workforce,

asr-003174
03:06:44.000 --> 03:06:48.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: 25.395 billion funds,

asr-003175
03:06:48.000 --> 03:06:50.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: the national health workforce,

asr-003176
03:06:50.000 --> 03:06:52.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: support system,

asr-003177
03:06:52.000 --> 03:06:57.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: which deploys doctors, nurses, midwives,

asr-003178
03:06:57.000 --> 03:06:59.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and allied health professionals

asr-003179
03:06:59.000 --> 03:07:03.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: to the communities that need them most.

asr-003180
03:07:03.000 --> 03:07:05.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: For medical assistance,

asr-003181
03:07:05.000 --> 03:07:09.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: 24.239 billion funds,

asr-003182
03:07:09.000 --> 03:07:16.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: medical assistance to indigent and financially incapacitated patients.

asr-003183
03:07:16.000 --> 03:07:19.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: This is the program behind the Malasakit Centers,

asr-003184
03:07:19.000 --> 03:07:22.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: it stands between a poor family

asr-003185
03:07:22.000 --> 03:07:26.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and a financial ruin when illness strikes,

asr-003186
03:07:26.000 --> 03:07:31.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and this is consistent with Republic Act No. 11463

asr-003187
03:07:31.000 --> 03:07:36.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and Republic Act No. 8344.

asr-003188
03:07:36.000 --> 03:07:38.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: For health facilities,

asr-003189
03:07:38.000 --> 03:07:43.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: 14.540 billion,

asr-003190
03:07:43.000 --> 03:07:48.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Health Facilities Enhancement Program, or HFEP,

asr-003191
03:07:48.000 --> 03:07:51.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: for the construction, upgrading,

asr-003192
03:07:51.000 --> 03:07:55.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and equipping of government health facilities

asr-003193
03:07:55.000 --> 03:08:00.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: under Republic Act No. 11223.

asr-003194
03:08:00.000 --> 03:08:02.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: For essential commodities,

asr-003195
03:08:02.000 --> 03:08:08.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: 9.095 billion procures commodities for family health,

asr-003196
03:08:08.000 --> 03:08:12.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: immunization, and nutrition protecting our mothers,

asr-003197
03:08:12.000 --> 03:08:16.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: newborns, and children.

asr-003198
03:08:16.000 --> 03:08:18.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: For cancer care,

asr-003199
03:08:18.000 --> 03:08:21.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: 3.751 billion funds,

asr-003200
03:08:21.000 --> 03:08:23.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: the Cancer Assistance Fund,

asr-003201
03:08:23.000 --> 03:08:26.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and 1.314 billion funds,

asr-003202
03:08:26.000 --> 03:08:28.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: cancer control commodities

asr-003203
03:08:28.000 --> 03:08:32.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: under the National Integrated Cancer Control Program,

asr-003204
03:08:32.000 --> 03:08:37.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and this is pursuant to Republic Act No. 11215.

asr-003205
03:08:37.000 --> 03:08:39.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: For emergency response,

asr-003206
03:08:39.000 --> 03:08:44.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: 500 million capitalizes the Quick Response Fund,

asr-003207
03:08:44.000 --> 03:08:48.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: ready for health response to calamities

asr-003208
03:08:48.000 --> 03:08:51.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and disease outbreaks.

asr-003209
03:08:51.000 --> 03:08:53.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The Department will carry the entire program

asr-003210
03:08:53.000 --> 03:09:03.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: with a complement of 99,143 authorized positions.

asr-003211
03:09:03.000 --> 03:09:05.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The measure carries special provisions

asr-003212
03:09:05.000 --> 03:09:08.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: that keep faith with our people.

asr-003213
03:09:08.000 --> 03:09:11.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Hospital income is retained for hospital use.

asr-003214
03:09:11.000 --> 03:09:13.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Health workers are deployed

asr-003215
03:09:13.000 --> 03:09:18.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: with priority to fourth and fifth class municipalities,

asr-003216
03:09:18.000 --> 03:09:21.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: geographically isolated areas,

asr-003217
03:09:21.000 --> 03:09:23.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and indigenous communities.

asr-003218
03:09:23.000 --> 03:09:25.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Recipients of medical assistance

asr-003219
03:09:25.000 --> 03:09:27.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: are reported publicly

asr-003220
03:09:27.000 --> 03:09:31.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: in aggregated and anonymized form

asr-003221
03:09:31.000 --> 03:09:37.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: in compliance with Republic Act No. 10173.

asr-003222
03:09:37.000 --> 03:09:38.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Madam Speaker,

asr-003223
03:09:38.000 --> 03:09:42.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: this budget funds the hospitals our people rely on,

asr-003224
03:09:42.000 --> 03:09:45.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: the workers who staff them,

asr-003225
03:09:45.000 --> 03:09:48.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: the medicines that save lives,

asr-003226
03:09:48.000 --> 03:09:51.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and the assistance that keeps sickness

asr-003227
03:09:51.000 --> 03:09:54.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: from becoming poverty.

asr-003228
03:09:54.000 --> 03:09:58.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: With 61% directed to the regions,

asr-003229
03:09:58.000 --> 03:10:04.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: this budget brings care closer to the Filipinos

asr-003230
03:10:04.000 --> 03:10:06.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: who need it most.

asr-003231
03:10:06.000 --> 03:10:09.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: On behalf of the Committee on Appropriation,

asr-003232
03:10:09.000 --> 03:10:11.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: this representation,

asr-003233
03:10:11.000 --> 03:10:15.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: together with Vice Chair Angela Garcia,

asr-003234
03:10:15.000 --> 03:10:18.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: respectfully commend to this House,

asr-003235
03:10:18.000 --> 03:10:21.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: the Fiscal Year 2027 budget

asr-003236
03:10:21.000 --> 03:10:25.000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: of the Department of Health and PhilHealth

asr-003237
03:10:25.000 --> 03:10:29.000
